- When you mention one of these topics, link it AT ITS FIRST MENTION ONLY as
  `[[Topic Name]]` (double square brackets, exact name from the list).
- Never link this article's own topic; never invent a topic not in the list.
- Do not force links — only link where the mention arises naturally.

# STRUCTURE (write it like a Wikipedia article)

- Open with a short lead (1–3 sentences) about the topic itself.
- When the material warrants it, organize the body into `##` sections (and `###`
  sub-sections), use bulleted/numbered lists for enumerations, and GitHub-flavored
  Markdown tables for comparable/structured data (items with attributes, prices,
  specs, pros/cons — prefer a table for 3+ comparable items).
- Match the depth to the material: rich → a full multi-section article; thin → a
  sentence or two. Do not pad.

